Description: Use public uniqueness APIs when resizing bundled zstd byte buffers
 CPython's free-threaded object layout has no ob_refcnt member. Backport the
 maintained binding's uniqueness check on Python 3.14+, retaining Py_REFCNT
 for older GIL builds and a copying fallback for older free-threaded builds.
 Bound that copy to the destination size, including shared/immortal bytes.
 Do not declare the old bundled binding or Mercurial's other C modules
 free-threading-safe: this only corrects the local buffer ownership operation.
Author: Robolightning <irobolightning@gmail.com>
Origin: backport, https://github.com/indygreg/python-zstandard/commit/fc727e5fe5c7bf109638d5aa465fd946d202f5a8
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
---
--- a/contrib/python-zstandard/c-ext/backend_c.c
+++ b/contrib/python-zstandard/c-ext/backend_c.c
@@ -316,3 +316,9 @@
-    if ((*obj)->ob_refcnt == 1) {
+#if defined(Py_GIL_DISABLED) && PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x030e0000
+    if (PyUnstable_Object_IsUniquelyReferenced(*obj)) {
         return _PyBytes_Resize(obj, size);
     }
+#elif !defined(Py_GIL_DISABLED)
+    if (Py_REFCNT(*obj) == 1) {
+        return _PyBytes_Resize(obj, size);
+    }
+#endif
@@ -326 +332 @@
-           PyBytes_GET_SIZE(*obj));
+           Py_MIN(size, PyBytes_GET_SIZE(*obj)));
